<h1>Lento Privacy Policy</h1>
<p class="text-sm text-gray-400">Effective date: November 3, 2026</p>

<p>
    Lento is provided by Euler Soft. This policy
    explains what Lento processes, why it is processed, where it is stored, and the choices available to you.
    Lento is a wellness app. It does not provide medical advice, diagnosis, or treatment.
</p>

<h2>Information Stored on Your Device</h2>
<p>
    Your fasts and fasting plans, weight and body measurements, check-ins (such as mood, hunger, energy,
    focus, stress, cravings, sleep, and symptoms), habits, notes, and settings are stored on your iPhone and,
    if you use it, your Apple Watch. Progress photos are stored only on your device, with iOS file protection,
    are excluded from device backups, and are never uploaded by Lento. Local data remains until you delete it
    in Lento (Profile &gt; Privacy &gt; Delete all data) or uninstall the app.
</p>

<h2>Apple Health</h2>
<p>
    With your permission, Lento reads weight, body fat percentage, waist circumference, and sleep from Apple
    Health to show your progress, and writes the entries you choose to share. Health data is never used for
    advertising or marketing and is never sold. It leaves your device only if you turn on &quot;Lento Cloud
    Sync&quot; (below), which includes weight entries that came from Apple Health. You can change Health
    permissions at any time in the iOS Settings or Health app.
</p>

<h2>Lento Cloud Sync (Optional)</h2>
<p>
    If you turn on &quot;Sync to Lento cloud&quot; in Profile &gt; Privacy, your fasts, weight entries,
    check-ins, and habits (including notes, shortened to 1,000 characters) are copied to Euler Soft&apos;s
    database on Cloudflare. The copy is linked to this installation of Lento through an anonymous identifier,
    not to an account, so it cannot be moved to another device or to a new installation. Progress photos and
    body measurements are not synced. Turning sync off stops uploads; records already on the server stay
    there until you use &quot;Delete all data&quot;, which erases them from the server as well as from your
    device.
</p>

<h2>Live Activity and Notifications</h2>
<p>
    To keep the Lock Screen Live Activity and its fasting stages up to date, Lento sends the Live Activity
    push token, the start, goal, and stage times of your current fast, your streak, the Live Activity
    labels in your language, and your time zone to Euler Soft&apos;s server, which sends updates through
    Apple Push Notification service. Only your most recent fasts are kept; older records are removed
    automatically. Reminders you schedule are created
    on your device.
</p>

<h2>Device Security and Identifiers</h2>
<p>
    Lento creates an anonymous user identifier on Euler Soft&apos;s server for this installation, bound to a
    device key from Apple App Attest. It is not linked to your name, email address, Apple ID, or purchases. Requests are protected with Apple App Attest and Firebase App Check, which
    confirm they come from a genuine copy of Lento, and with encrypted connections to a pinned server
    certificate. The anonymous identifier is used to prevent abuse and to keep your synced data and Live
    Activity records separate from other users.
</p>

<h2>Purchases and Subscriptions</h2>
<p>
    Apple processes payments. Lento and RevenueCat process product identifiers, subscription and entitlement
    status, transaction identifiers, and purchase history to unlock Pro, restore purchases, and provide
    support. Euler Soft&apos;s server does not receive purchase information. Lento never receives your
    payment-card details.
</p>

<h2>Analytics and Crash Reports</h2>
<p>
    Anonymous usage analytics (Firebase Analytics) are off unless you turn on &quot;Share anonymous
    analytics&quot; in Profile &gt; Privacy. When on, they record which screens and features are used, never
    your health entries. Crash reports (Firebase Crashlytics) include technical information such as the
    device model, iOS version, and the steps that led to a crash, to help fix problems. Lento does not track
    you across other companies&apos; apps or websites and does not show ads.
</p>

<h2>Purposes</h2>
<ul>
    <li>Track fasts, weight, body measurements, check-ins, habits, and progress photos</li>
    <li>Sync and restore your data when you turn sync on</li>
    <li>Keep the Live Activity, widgets, and Apple Watch up to date</li>
    <li>Authenticate requests and protect the service from abuse</li>
    <li>Complete and restore purchases</li>
    <li>Fix crashes and, with your permission, understand feature use</li>
</ul>

<h2>Service Providers</h2>
<ul>
    <li>Cloudflare for Euler Soft&apos;s server, database, security, and request handling</li>
    <li>Google Firebase for App Check, crash reports, and opt-in analytics</li>
    <li>RevenueCat for subscription and entitlement management</li>
    <li>Apple for the App Store, StoreKit, Apple Health, App Attest, and push notifications</li>
</ul>
<p>
    These providers process information under their own terms, privacy policies, and security controls.
    Processing may occur outside your country, subject to legally required transfer safeguards. Euler Soft
    does not sell or share personal information for advertising.
</p>

<h2>Retention and Deletion</h2>
<p>
    Synced records stay on the server
    until you delete them or use &quot;Delete all data&quot;, which removes every record linked to your
    anonymous identifier from the server (an internet connection is needed for that part). If Lento is not opened
    for 13 months, the anonymous identifier and every record linked to it are deleted from the server
    automatically. Limited security records are kept only as long as needed to prevent abuse. Provider-held crash, analytics, and purchase records follow each
    provider&apos;s retention settings.
</p>
<p>
    You can download a copy of your data in Profile &gt; Privacy &gt; Download my data, and you can ask
    Euler Soft for access to or deletion of server-side information using the contact below.
</p>

<h2>Your Choices</h2>
<ul>
    <li>Allow or decline Apple Health, notification, and Face ID access</li>
    <li>Turn Lento cloud sync on or off</li>
    <li>Turn anonymous analytics on or off</li>
    <li>Download or delete all of your data in the app</li>
    <li>Manage or cancel subscriptions in your Apple ID settings</li>
</ul>

<h2>Security</h2>
<p>
    Lento uses encrypted connections with certificate pinning, Apple App Attest, Firebase App Check, iOS data
    protection, optional Face ID locks for the app and for progress photos, and per-user access controls on
    the server. No method of storage or transmission can guarantee absolute security.
</p>

<h2>Age Requirement</h2>
<p>
    Lento is intended for adults aged 18 or older. Fasting is not suitable for everyone; talk to a healthcare
    professional before fasting if you are pregnant, breastfeeding, have a medical condition, or take
    medication. Euler Soft does not knowingly collect personal information from children.
</p>

<h2>Policy Changes</h2>
<p>
    This policy may change when features, providers, or legal obligations change. The effective date will be
    updated when material changes are published.
</p>

<h2>Contact</h2>
<p>
    For privacy questions or requests, contact
    <a href="mailto:eulersoft@outlook.com">eulersoft@outlook.com</a>.
</p>
